# Auto detect text files and perform LF normalization
* text=auto

# Custom for Visual Studio
*.cs     diff=csharp

# Standard to msysgit
*.doc	 diff=astextplain
*.DOC	 diff=astextplain
*.docx diff=astextplain
*.DOCX diff=astextplain
*.dot  diff=astextplain
*.DOT  diff=astextplain
*.pdf  diff=astextplain
*.PDF	 diff=astextplain
*.rtf	 diff=astextplain
*.RTF	 diff=astextplain

# [XPLAT] migrated from net48/WinForms - byte-stable fixtures for cross-OS golden/parity tests
# (see MIGRATION_DOCS/PARITY_REPORT.md). The migration adds golden-file BYTE-COMPARISON parity
# tests (AAP 0.6.4) that run on a windows / ubuntu / macos CI matrix. Any file taking part in a
# byte-for-byte round-trip/golden comparison must NOT be EOL-converted by Git, so the bytes on
# disk equal the committed bytes on every OS. The "-text" attribute disables Git's CRLF<->LF
# normalization entirely (for a pure-binary blob, "binary" is the equivalent "-text -diff"
# shorthand). These rules are PATH-SCOPED to test/fixture directories only; the global
# "* text=auto" above still governs ordinary source, docs, and config, and a more specific
# path rule here intentionally overrides it for the fixtures listed below.

# Existing settings golden fixture: AgLibrary.Tests reads this file back and asserts it equals
# the freshly-saved output (round-trip byte-compare in
# XmlSettingsHandlerTests.SaveXMLFile_ShouldSaveWithoutException).
SourceCode/AgLibrary.Tests/Settings/TestSettings.xml  -text

# New parity golden artifacts created under the AgOpenGPS.Tests parity suite (PGN frame .bin,
# field-file round-trips, ISOXML V3/V4, settings round-trips). Parity/ is a dedicated
# fixture+test directory, so pin everything beneath it to keep every committed golden artifact
# byte-identical across operating systems, whatever its extension.
SourceCode/AgOpenGPS.Tests/Parity/**  -text

# Field-file test data and ISOXML exports used by the parity suite, pinned anywhere within the
# parity test project regardless of fixture subfolder layout. Field formats are plain-text .txt
# (Boundary, Contour, Elevation, Field, Flags, Headland, Headlines, RecPath, Sections,
# TrackLines, Tram); ISOXML exports are .xml. Scoped to the test project only - NOT a repo-wide
# *.txt / *.xml rule.
SourceCode/AgOpenGPS.Tests/**/*.txt  -text
SourceCode/AgOpenGPS.Tests/**/*.xml  -text
